{#
  Home page. Composes the frame (layouts/base.njk brings the masthead and
  colophon) and the locked components. Copy lives in front matter so it stays
  editable without touching markup.

  Two deliberate departures from the handoff, both noted for review:

  1. The handoff sets BOTH the proposition and the "Get Built. Get Found."
     tagline as h1. Two h1 elements on one page is wrong for assistive tech and
     for search. The proposition is the h1 because it describes the page; the
     tagline is display type, not a document heading, and it already repeats in
     the colophon on every page, so it renders as a paragraph.
  2. No alt-glyph anywhere on this page, per instruction. The handoff carries
     .alt-dot on the O of "Found" in the hero tagline. The colophon keeps its
     own swap, since that belongs to the frame rather than to this page.
#}
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}
{% from "components/section.njk" import section %}
{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}
{% from "components/icon.njk" import icon %}

{% call container(class="cs-hero") %}
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--hero-h" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--hero-v" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="cs-hero__grid">
    <div class="cs-hero__copy">
      <h1 class="cs-hero__headline">The web has changed. We’ve been ahead of it since 2011.</h1>
      <p class="cs-hero__lede">
        Your customers don’t just Google you, they check Yelp, ask AI, and decide in
        seconds. We help service businesses and brands get found everywhere it happens.
      </p>
      {{ button("See how we work", href="/what-we-do/", class="cs-hero__cta") }}
    </div>

    <img class="cs-hero__figure"
         src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-seed-portrait.webp"
         alt="Seed, high-contrast black and white with a single madder bar"
         width="440" height="550"
         loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
  </div>

  <p class="cs-hero__tagline">Get Built. Get Found.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call container() %}
  <ul class="cs-proofband">
    {% for item in proof %}
      <li class="cs-proofband__item">
        {{ icon(item.icon) }}
        <span class="cs-proofband__label">{{ item.label }}</span>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call section() %}
  <div class="cs-duo">
    {% for service in services %}
      <div class="cs-duo__item">
        <h2>{{ service.title }}</h2>
        <p>{{ service.body }}</p>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {{ button("See what we do", href="/what-we-do/", variant="ghost", arrow=true, class="mt-10") }}
{% endcall %}

<div class="cs-espalier">
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--espalier cs-rule--espalier-l" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--espalier cs-rule--espalier-r" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% call container(class="relative") %}
    <img class="cs-espalier__figure"
         src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-espalier-1-landscape.webp"
         alt="Espalier, growth trained to a deliberate shape"
         width="1120" height="220"
         loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <div class="cs-espalier__arc" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{% call container(narrow=true, class="py-24") %}
  <blockquote class="cs-pullquote m-0">
    Steve and Connor don’t upsell you. They aligned perfectly with our objective to
    create an enduring online presence.
    <cite>Alex Loveless, Executive Director, The Admissions Angle</cite>
  </blockquote>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(class="cs-close") %}
  <p class="cs-close__note">
    We keep the roster small so senior people do the work. Booking for Q3 is open;
    if the timing is right for your business, let’s talk.
  </p>
  {{ button("Start a conversation", href="/contact/") }}
{% endcall %}
